lib/Langertha/Skeid.pm uses File::ShareDir; lib/Langertha/Skeid/KeyBroker/OpenBao.pm uses namespace::clean and HTTP::Tiny. None are declared in cpanfile. namespace::clean and File::ShareDir are not core, so a clean-perl install of the tarball fails at runtime, not at install time.

Fix: declare them. Then grep every use statement in lib/ and bin/ against the cpanfile rather than trusting it.
Fixed: File::ShareDir, namespace::clean, HTTP::Tiny declared in cpanfile.
